# PORT-SUN-ROTATION: a directional light is aimed by its Rotation (forward -Z), as UE's ULightComponent::GetDirection;
# Translation no longer encodes a direction. Every scene/prefab is raised by the light chain (LGHT v1, SceneMigrator
# MigrateLightRotationV0ToV1). Details shows ONE direction widget on the sun: compass + horizon arc + Elevation/Azimuth.
# The Starter sun is entity 13376537502658031226 ("Sun"); after the migration its Translation is 0,0,0.
Дано run Scene "Open Scene Starter.desce"
Дано run Entity "Sun"
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.FOV 60
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,400,1500
Дано --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-0.2,-1
# Details scrolled with the mouse wheel down to the Sun Direction widget (it sits below Transform/Light/Atmosphere).
Дано input scroll Details 150,300 -10
# The cursor off Details, so no field tooltip covers the widget.
Дано input move - 1000,1100
Тогда 1_migrated frame and shadows as on dev before the migration (the sun lights from the same place); Details on Sun shows the Sun Direction widget
# The widget's Elevation number, through the same rule (Rules::SunAngles -> AimDirectionalLight, one undo step).
Когда --subject selection set SunElevation 5
Тогда 2_low_sun long shadows; Details: the whole direction widget in view (compass + horizon arc + Elevation/Azimuth), Elevation 5.0, no second direction control
# The horizon, looking towards the sun: Elevation 5 / Azimuth 54.5 = towards +X+Z (0.811, 0, 0.579), past the fire VFX.
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,300,0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.811,0.0,0.579
Тогда-вид 2b_horizon sunset sky, the sun disc just above the horizon
# A REAL drag on the rotate gizmo's world-Y (azimuth) ring, seen from above. The camera clamps its pitch short of
# straight down (Direction reads back 0,-0.99985,-0.01745 = pitch -89), so the gizmo centre is NOT the viewport
# centre: measured at ~(715.5, 451) pt, ring radius ~86 pt. The end point was tuned live against the readback:
# 801.5,451 -> 719,365 turns the light's azimuth -125.54 -> -36.01 = 89.5 deg (Space: World; snap off).
Когда run Transform Rotate
Когда run Transform "Space: World"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,1500,0
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-1,-0.0001
Когда --subject viewport drag 801.5,451 719,365 24
Тогда 3_gizmo shadows turned by 90 deg (seen from above); the widget shows the azimuth changed by 90
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 0,400,1500
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0,-0.2,-1
Когда run Action Undo
Когда run Action Undo
Тогда 4_undo frame as 1_migrated
